A listing in a shopping agent's cart has just sold out. Find replacements for that cart line among the other listing records shown, with these reading rules: the listing's attribute for a property decides when its key names that same property (any key spelling, one element of a list is enough, synonyms and unit conversions count, a value containing the required value's words counts, such as "deep teal" for teal, limits include the edge); a key for a different property, even a related one (a handle colour is not the body's colour), decides nothing; when no attribute names that property, the wanted value stated under another attribute or in the title or description counts (a bare figure that does not say what it measures counts for nothing); a requirement the category label itself states is met by that category; the category label must match the item; a rule of being unlike another listing's value counts as met unless the records show that same value; out-of-stock listings and listings that break the budget do not fit.
Return ONE JSON object and nothing else: {"fits": [{"id": listing id, "price": its price as a number as the record shows it} for every listing that appears to meet every requirement of the sold-out line's item, at most 6], "reason": "one sentence"}

REQUEST:
Up at my Tennessee college, I've got a scholarship banquet where I'll be shaking hands and getting photographed (first time for me, y'all). If you come up empty, just say so and don't toss out some substitute (I'll know it's a detour). Now, I'm skeptical of most of what's out there, but fair is fair: show me luxury & formal watches in the green color family (I'll check the color myself, don't worry). And it's got to be something you actually have on hand, not just a listing sitting on some website way down the trail somewhere. Price tops out at 2750 cts, not a single one over (every penny counts for me, y'all, and student loans ain't gonna pay themselves). Total, you can send me 3 messages and no more than that. Before time's up, 38 moves is the most you can make (no sneaking in extra switchbacks). A green watch ought to look right on my wrist all evening, steady as a well-marked trail.

REQUIREMENTS IN FORCE:
- item: luxury & formal watches, quantity 1; requirements: none beyond the kind of product; shopper does not mind: finish, dial size, strap material
- budget: at most 2750 cents in total
- pick: any listing that fits everything
- in stock only
- wish (tie-breaker only): Watch looks right on the wrist all evening.
- rule from the request: Send at most 3 messages to the shopper.
- rule from the request: Use at most 38 moves, with no extra steps.
- rule from the request: If nothing fits, say so plainly without substitutes.
- rule from the request: Only buy items actually in stock on hand.
- if nothing fits: end without naming or suggesting any listing
- listing attributes come from datasheet_for_item; view_listing show none; a listing's page (what a chain of pages or a page check means) is shown by view_listing

